-- the two rows as landed, verbatim:
| a search or glob returns nothing and you are about to report a file as ABSENT / MISSING | **A search that returns nothing is a reading of the SEARCH, not of the tree.** A null result is not evidence of absence: report it as *"no match under pattern `<the pattern>`"* and NAME the pattern, because absence is a claim about the tree and needs a search that could have found it. Measured instance (2026-09-17): the glob `evidence/{team-watchdog,review}/**/{20260917T081003Z-t13/REVIEW.md,20260917T084000Z-t30/result.json}` returned nothing while BOTH files existed at `evidence/pack-closure/review-B/20260917T081003Z-t13/REVIEW.md` (15,381 B, sha256 `810830adda53…`) and `evidence/pack-closure/review-B/20260917T084000Z-t30/result.json` (11,600 B, sha256 `f6b06c5c1e13…`) — the narrow pattern was the error, and widening it before reporting is what kept a false "missing" out of the record. *Attribution: the operational phrasing ("no match under pattern `<…>`", never "absent") is the Architect's; the measured instances and this row's text are lane C's.* |
| a path or number quoted in a REPORT does not resolve / does not reproduce | **Cite the reading AND the sentence that carries it; when the sentence is not the reader's, say whose it is.** The reading and the sentence that carries it are separate facts, so a provenance record names all three owners — first-party reading, first-party runs, second-hand wording. Worked example on disk: `evidence/team-watchdog/lane-c-2a/20260917T074144Z/raw/readings.log` ADDENDUM 11 (a first-party reading of `scripts/mpd-bg.mjs` by the Architect) + ADDENDUM 14 (the ownership split: first-party reading / first-party runs by lane C / the second-hand sentence, marked as not reviewed by its subject). For anything destined for a REPORT, the companion rule is FULL PATH OR NO CITATION: the abbreviations `review-B/…` and `lane-c-2a/…` fail `-e` while the three full paths above resolve (measured 2026-09-17). *Attribution: the rule sentence is the Architect's; the ADDENDUM 11/14 split, the `-e` measurement and this row's text are lane C's.* |

